window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-510b5c3c8b722b3e"]={"key":"ny_c-510b5c3c8b722b3e","group":"ny_c","uid":"510b5c3c8b722b3e","rank":22,"title":"coldharbour counterposition sequence memo","occupation":"real_estate_brokers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are Arjun Fitzgerald, the listing broker advising Reina Whitcombe and Inglewood Board on the sale of the 96,000-square-foot Coldharbour Provisions cold-storage plant in Illinois to Underhill Solutions, whose deal team and financing are based in Indiana. Eleven days before Reina’s 1031 identification deadline, Underhill has re-traded for a $780,000 “credit,” pointing to the refrigeration and roof reports. The timing and pattern of its requests may indicate lender re-underwriting, but nobody has confirmed that, and Reina needs her 60-day use of the loading annex after closing more than she needs to preserve every dollar of headline price. Eamon Kristiansen, who was trying to keep the deal together, has already told Underhill informally that “we’ll make the report items right,” even though neither the scope nor his authority was settled. The word “credit” is also being used in the correspondence to mean both a reduction in purchase price and a seller credit shown at closing, and Jelena Demirci will not approve a position that leaves that ambiguity unresolved. Use the complete transaction record in `coldharbour_transaction_evidence.pdf` to prepare the counter-position and concession sequence Reina can authorize before Thursday’s call. Tell Eamon, who is covering the call and has not previously worked on this transaction, what Inglewood Board will give, the order in which he may give it, what must be obtained in return, where he must stop, and what he must never offer. The memorandum must make one coherent counter-position, address the Illinois and Indiana implications relevant to the transaction without presenting legal or tax advice, and distinguish supported facts from negotiation inferences. Make every monetary figure, date, property term, and report-based assertion traceable to the evidence bundle; do not create estimates or deal terms that are not there. Keep the memorandum to no more than six pages, including any tables or appendices, and make it usable during the call without Eamon having to ask you what to say next. Write the final file into the top level of the working directory using exactly the filename `coldharbour_counterposition_memo.docx`.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/coldharbour_transaction_evidence.pdf` — Complete mixed-format evidence bundle containing the transaction terms, inspection materials, correspondence, call notes, authority limits, deadline information, leaseback requirements, and jurisdiction-related compliance material needed to prepare the counter-position.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `coldharbour_counterposition_memo.docx` — A call-ready counter-position and concession-sequence memorandum for owner authorization and compliance review. (Must be written to the top level of the working directory under the exact filename; must not exceed six pages including tables and appendices; must present one coherent counter-position; all figures, dates, property terms, and report assertions must be traceable to the supplied evidence bundle.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/coldharbour_transaction_evidence.pdf","bytes":14696,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/64853bbe50087007a90d01ec34bda08d7e26bdfd74c58332f9d8bcd82069a73d.pdf","sha256":"64853bbe50087007a90d01ec34bda08d7e26bdfd74c58332f9d8bcd82069a73d","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"             Coldharbour Provisions Transaction Evidence Bundle\n Compiled for Inglewood Board | status as of May 13, 2026 | exhibit-indexed source record\n\n\n Index\n   Exhibit        Record                                                      Date / source\n\n   A              Executed Purchase Agreement abstract                        Apr. 3, 2026\n\n   B              Owner priority and annex term sheet                         May 8, 2026\n\n   C              Polar Mechanical refrigeration assessment                   Apr. 24, 2026\n\n   D              Northline Roof Consulting report excerpt                    Apr. 26, 2026\n\n   E              Buyer correspondence and call notes                         May 4-12, 2026\n\n   F              Current authority record                                    May 13, 2026\n\n   G              Compliance routing note                                     May 12, 2026\n\n Source-use note. This bundle combines transaction records and limited excerpts. It records what was said and reported; it does not\n determine legal responsibility, engineering scope, tax treatment, or lender approval.\n\n\n\n\nColdharbour transaction record | Confidential working file                                                                    Page 1\n\f EXHIBIT A | Executed Purchase Agreement Abstract\n Property: Coldharbour Provisions cold-storage plant, 96,000 square feet, 1450 Coldharbour Road, Joliet, Illinois. Seller: Reina\n Whitcombe and Inglewood Board. Buyer: Underhill Solutions, Inc.. Purchase price: $18,400,000. Agreement signed April 3, 2026.\n\n   Term                      Abstracted provision\n\n   Closing                   Closing is scheduled for May 29, 2026, subject to written amendment signed by Seller and Buyer.\n\n   Inspection                Buyer inspection period expired May 1, 2026. Reports delivered during that period are not an\n                             agreement to repair or a seller warranty.\n\n   Changes                   No change to price, credit, repair obligation, possession, or closing may be effective unless stated in a\n                             signed written amendment.\n\n   Release / survival        At closing, Buyer releases Seller from pre-closing property-condition claims except obligations\n                             expressly preserved in the closing documents. No condition warranty survives unless expressly written.\n\n   Closing documents         Any seller credit must be reflected in the closing statement and documented in the amendment; a\n                             purchase-price reduction changes the contract price.\n\n EXHIBIT A-2 | Milestone sheet\n   Milestone                             Date / time                                                  Owner\n\n   Covering-broker call                  Thursday, May 14, 2026, 10:00 a.m. CT                        Eamon Kristiansen\n\n   Proposed package expiry               5:00 p.m. CT on Friday, May 15, 2026                         If issued\n\n   1031 identification deadline          May 25, 2026                                                 Reina / qualified intermediary\n\n   Scheduled closing                     May 29, 2026                                                 Seller / Buyer\n\n The identification deadline is 11 calendar days after the May 14 call. The agreement does not make the 1031 exchange a Buyer\n contingency.\n\n\n\n\nColdharbour transaction record | Confidential working file                                                                               Page 2\n\f EXHIBIT B | Owner Priority Record and Annex Term Sheet\n May 8 owner instruction from Reina Whitcombe to Arjun Fitzgerald: “The annex is how we keep receiving our last outbound orders.\n I need the 60 days after closing. I can trade money to protect that, but I will not close and then hope they let us use it.”\n Inglewood Board minute: preserve uninterrupted post-closing loading-annex use ahead of headline-price preservation; no\n independent broker authority to waive, defer, or alter the annex arrangement.\n\n   Annex term                     Agreed business instruction for proposed amendment\n\n   Space / period                 east loading annex (approximately 8,000 square feet); May 30, 2026 through July 28, 2026 (60\n                                  days).\n\n   Access                         Seller personnel and carriers retain 24/7 dock and truck-court access through the east gate; Buyer\n                                  may reasonably coordinate safety and site rules.\n\n   Operations / cost              Seller operates only the annex, pays its own labor, utilities measured to the annex submeter, and\n                                  routine cleanup. No rent is charged for the 60-day period.\n\n   Insurance / risk               Seller maintains commercial general liability and workers compensation for its operations and is\n                                  responsible for loss caused by its personnel; Buyer carries property coverage for the building.\n\n   Turnover                       Seller returns the annex broom-clean, removes inventory and temporary equipment by 6:00 p.m.\n                                  CT July 28, and delivers keys/cards; no holdover right.\n\n EXHIBIT B-2 | Available non-price responses\n Seller may make available the Polar and Northline source files, provide a single escorted pre-closing access window for buyer\n consultants, assign any transferable roof contractor workmanship warranty without representation as to transferability, and consider\n a targeted cure or escrow only in a signed package. These are options, not promises.\n\n\n\n\nColdharbour transaction record | Confidential working file                                                                             Page 3\n\f EXHIBIT C | Polar Mechanical Refrigeration Assessment (Apr. 24, 2026)\n Scope: visual inspection and operating review of accessible components only. Polar did not perform destructive testing, pressure\n testing, refrigerant analysis, code review, or an assessment of non-accessible piping. Costs are planning allowances, not bids.\n\n   Finding category             Report wording                                                         Amount / qualification\n\n   Observed condition           Corrosion and seepage were observed at three brine isolation-valve     No leak-rate or\n                                assemblies in the south machine room. System was operating at time     remaining-life conclusion.\n                                of visit.\n\n   Immediate                    Replace the three observed assemblies and reinsulate adjacent          Planning allowance\n   recommendation               disturbed pipe.                                                        $145,000; excludes\n                                                                                                       concealed conditions,\n                                                                                                       abatement, controls\n                                                                                                       integration, and downtime.\n\n   Further investigation        Before work, verify pipe wall thickness and insulation condition at    Could change scope; not\n                                opened locations.                                                      priced.\n\n   Future recommendation        Consider a system-wide valve modernization plan in the next capital    Not identified as immediate\n                                cycle.                                                                 work; no project estimate.\n\n EXHIBIT D | Northline Roof Consulting Excerpt (Apr. 26, 2026)\n Scope: visual walkover of accessible roof areas; no moisture scan, core cuts, deck testing, or destructive investigation. This is a\n condition opinion, not a roof warranty or bid.\n\n   Finding category             Report wording                                                         Amount / qualification\n\n   Observed condition           Localized seam splits and flashing deterioration were observed in      Conditions may be\n                                roughly 12,000 square feet of the north membrane field. No active      weather-dependent.\n                                interior leak was observed during the visit.\n\n   Immediate                    Perform localized seam/flashing repairs within 12 months and inspect   Budgetary allowance\n   recommendation               after severe weather.                                                  $95,000; excludes wet\n                                                                                                       insulation, deck repair,\n                                                                                                       mobilization changes, and\n                                                                                                       taxes.\n\n   Lifecycle observation        Estimated remaining useful life: 3-5 years; plan for future membrane   Planning range $365,000;\n                                replacement.                                                           not a present repair\n                                                                                                       directive or bid.\n\n\n\n\nColdharbour transaction record | Confidential working file                                                                           Page 4\n\f EXHIBIT E | Buyer Correspondence and Call Notes\n May 4, 2026 | Underhill asset manager email: “We are assessing whether the roof and refrigeration items need a credit in the\n purchase price before we can finalize our closing model.”\n May 6, 2026 | Eamon Kristiansen call note: Eamon told Underhill’s deal lead, “we’ll make the report items right.” He recorded that he\n meant the parties would address documented items; no scope, amount, remedy, seller authority, or signed amendment was\n discussed or confirmed.\n May 8, 2026 | Underhill finance email: “Our Indiana financing team needs the consultant files and a clean statement of any seller\n contribution. Please separate roof from refrigeration and show the proposed treatment at closing.” No lender name, lender\n instruction, consultant report, or underwriting condition was attached.\n May 11, 2026 | Underhill deal lead email: “We need a $780,000 credit to stay on the May 29 closing path: $380,000 refrigeration\n reserve, $250,000 roof reserve, and $150,000 purchase-price re-trade.”\n May 12, 2026 | Call note: buyer asked whether “credit” could “show on the closing statement” if its lender required it. Buyer also\n asked for a consultant access window and the roof warranty file. The deal lead said the team needed an answer on Thursday. No\n person said a lender had ordered a credit.\n\n EXHIBIT E-2 | Demand reconciliation\n   Buyer label                                      Requested amount   Character as stated\n\n   Refrigeration reserve                            $380,000           Buyer-requested amount; not an accepted liability.\n\n   Roof reserve                                     $250,000           Buyer-requested amount; not an accepted liability.\n\n   Purchase-price re-trade                          $150,000           Buyer-requested amount; not an accepted liability.\n\n   Aggregate demand                                 $780,000           Buyer describes the aggregate as a “credit.”\n\n Record observation: the May 4 use of “credit in the purchase price” differs from the May 12 question about a contribution “on the\n closing statement.”\n\n\n\n\nColdharbour transaction record | Confidential working file                                                                       Page 5\n\f EXHIBIT F | Inglewood Board Authority Record (May 13, 2026)\n Purpose: call authority for May 14. This record supersedes informal broker messaging as an internal authorization record; it does\n not amend the Purchase Agreement.\n\n   Subject                             Authority / limitation\n\n   Maximum aggregate seller            Up to $240,000 total, only for a documented package tied to the reported immediate valve scope and\n   exposure                            localized roof repair scope. Seller-paid work, escrow, and any closing credit count toward one cap; no\n                                       stacking or double recovery.\n\n   Broker may discuss                  Report files, one escorted consultant-access window, transferable-warranty records, buyer’s\n                                       requested mechanics, and a conditional package. Eamon may not bind Seller.\n\n   Required conditions                 Executed annex agreement at or before a material economic concession; signed amendment; Buyer\n                                       release of the addressed report items; no warranty or future-performance assurance; unchanged May\n                                       29 closing unless Board approves otherwise.\n\n   Approvals                           Reina and Inglewood Board approve economics and annex changes; Jelena Demirci approves credit\n                                       terminology, compliance review, and final amendment package; Illinois counsel handles Illinois\n                                       real-estate documents and release language; tax adviser / qualified intermediary handles 1031; Buyer\n                                       and its lender confirm permitted closing-statement treatment.\n\n   Offer timing                        Any enhanced package may be offered only as a written, all-terms package expiring 5:00 p.m. CT on\n                                       Friday, May 15, 2026; if not accepted, the existing agreement remains in force without the enhanced\n                                       remedy.\n\n EXHIBIT G | Compliance Routing Note (May 12, 2026)\n Federal: the May 25 identification date is the seller’s stated federal 1031 timing milestone. Tax adviser and qualified intermediary,\n not the broker, must confirm identification and exchange consequences of any amendment or closing-statement item.\n Illinois: the real estate is in Joliet, Illinois. Illinois counsel should prepare or approve any amendment, annex possession/use\n agreement, property-condition release, and closing documentation affecting the Illinois property.\n Indiana: Underhill’s deal team and financing activity are based in Indiana. That location may explain who requests lender materials\n or a closing-statement format; it does not by itself determine the governing law for the Illinois real estate. Buyer and lender must\n confirm their financing requirements.\n Jelena Demirci: do not use “credit” in a counterproposal unless its mechanism is expressly defined as either a purchase-price\n reduction or a seller contribution shown at closing. Do not use it as a shorthand for both.\n\n\n\n\nColdharbour transaction record | Confidential working file                                                                                      Page 6\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/coldharbour_counterposition_memo.docx","bytes":43119,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/7816066e74e95666a792a2050a55005ecc504864b533bd77a8e0367eb903811b.docx","sha256":"7816066e74e95666a792a2050a55005ecc504864b533bd77a8e0367eb903811b","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"CALL AUTHORIZATION | COLDHARBOUR COUNTER-POSITION\nTo: Eamon Kristiansen, covering broker   |   From: Arjun Fitzgerald   |   Call: Thursday, May 14, 2026, 10:00 a.m. CT\n1. Decision to authorize before the call\nAuthorize one conditional package. Open with clarification and fact testing, not money. “Credit” in this memorandum means only a seller contribution shown on the closing statement; it is not a purchase-price reduction. The existing $18,400,000 contract price stays unchanged. [A; G]\nOpening position\nPrincipal boundary\nProvide the report files, one escorted consultant-access window, and transferable-warranty records; then consider a tightly documented package only after Underhill states its mechanism and substantiates the driver.\nNo binding economics. Final-stage aggregate seller exposure may not exceed $240,000 and must be a single closing-statement credit, seller-paid targeted work, or escrow within one cap, never stacked. [B-2; F]\n\nBuyer has asked for $780,000: $380,000 refrigeration reserve + $250,000 roof reserve + $150,000 purchase-price re-trade. Attribute this to Underhill; do not call it a liability. [E-2]\nNon-negotiable reciprocal term: execute the 60-day east loading annex (approximately 8,000 square feet) use agreement (May 30, 2026–July 28, 2026) before or simultaneously with any material economic concession. It is the reason not to spend economic leverage first. [B; F]\n2. Read this opening, then ask only these questions\nOpening language: “We have received the $780,000 request and the report materials. Before we discuss economics, I need to separate the requested remedy, the documented scope, and the closing mechanics so we can put forward one workable written package. We are prepared to address documented items in an authorized agreement, not make an open-ended commitment.”\nAsk\nWhy it changes the branch\n“When you say credit, do you mean a price reduction, a seller contribution shown on the closing statement, seller-paid work, or another mechanism?”\nPins down mechanics before value moves. [E; G]\n“Is a lender, lender consultant, or underwriting condition driving any item? Please identify it and send the directive, consultant requirement, or closing-statement instruction.”\nTests the lender hypothesis without alleging it. [E]\n“Which observed condition and which report recommendation supports each component, and who has authority to accept a documented package?”\nSeparates scope and decision-maker. [C; D; E]\n“What needs to be signed, and by when, to preserve the May 29 closing?”\nTests timing against the signed-document requirement. [A; E]\n\nInference, not fact: the May 8 request for a “clean statement” from Underhill’s Indiana financing team, the May 12 question about a closing-statement item, and the request for consultant files may be consistent with lender re-underwriting. No lender instruction or condition has been provided. [E]\n3. Ordered concession sequence | value only releases through the gate\nStage\nWhat Eamon may give or say\nMust obtain in return / stop\n1. Clarify\nAcknowledge the demand; provide existing Polar/Northline files, warranty records, and offer the one escorted access window. [B-2; F]\nObtain the mechanism, item-by-item support, decision-maker, timing, and lender evidence. STOP: no commitment while any of these is unresolved.\n2. Package the non-price response\nOffer a written conditional amendment concept: consultant access, transferable-warranty records without warranty of transferability, and a choice of targeted cure or escrow limited to the two immediate report scopes. [B-2; C; D; F]\nUnderhill must execute the annex agreement, confirm May 29 closing, release the addressed report items, and accept no future-performance warranty. Do not release items independently.\n3. Final authorized economics\nOnly if Underhill supplies lender-driven documentation and accepts the full package, say a seller contribution shown on the closing statement may be considered up to the single $240,000 cap, subject to Reina/Board approval, Jelena’s review, lender acceptance, and signed documents. [F]\nAnnex and amendment signed at or before the economic concession; one exclusive remedy, offset against seller-paid work or escrow, release, no price reduction, and May 29 closing retained. Offer expires 5:00 p.m. CT on Friday, May 15, 2026. [A; F]\n\nCap calculation: buyer request $780,000; Board authority $240,000; current report planning allowances $145,000 + $95,000 = $240,000. The lowest applicable limit is $240,000. The Polar and Northline figures are allowances, not bids or accepted liability. [C; D; F]\n4. Conditional call branches\nIf Underhill...\nEamon’s authorized response\nsubstantiates a lender-driven requirement\n“Send the identified condition and mechanics. Subject to review, we can circulate the documented package described above. The annex agreement, release, closing schedule, and exclusive-remedy treatment travel with it.” Do not name a dollar amount before approvals.\ncannot substantiate a lender driver\n“We can make the records and access available, and we can evaluate a targeted, documented response in the written package. We are not revising price or agreeing to a cash contribution on this call.” Keep value at Stages 1-2.\ninsists on the full $780,000 now\n“I do not have authority to agree to $780,000 or to a price reduction or closing credit on this call. Please provide the item support and lender basis; I will take a complete package for review.” Pause and escalate to Arjun, Reina/Board, and Jelena. [E-2; F]\nuses schedule or seller timing to demand an immediate answer\n“We are working to the May 29 schedule, but any change requires a reviewed written package. We can turn the requested materials and a package discussion promptly; I cannot improvise an amendment.” Do not mention Reina’s 1031 pressure. [A; F]\n\n5. Guardrails and controlled clarification\nNever give\nReason / source\nNever give an unconditional purchase-price reduction or closing credit before the annex right and all package conditions are secured.\nThe agreement price remains unchanged unless amended; annex is the owner priority. [A; B; F]\nNever give an uncapped or open-ended obligation to repair report items.\nReports contain exclusions, further investigation, future work, and planning allowances. [C; D; F]\nNever give broad assurances about the roof, refrigeration system, or future performance.\nNeither report is a warranty; the agreement limits survival absent writing. [A; C; D]\nNever sacrifice or defer the 60-day annex right in exchange for keeping the sale alive.\nOwner instruction makes it essential. [B]\nNever waive the signed-amendment, release, May 29 closing, or closing-document safeguards.\nThey are express Board conditions. [A; F]\n\nTruthful clarification of Eamon’s earlier statement: “I did say we would make the report items right. I am not withdrawing that; I am clarifying that the seller will address documented, authorized items through a written agreement. We did not settle scope, amount, remedy, or a warranty in that conversation.” The May 6 statement is acknowledged, but it is not a settled scope, dollar commitment, admission, or warranty. [E; F]\n6. Report discipline, roles, and timing\nRecord item\nCall treatment\nRefrigeration: observed corrosion/seepage at three valve assemblies; immediate replacement allowance $145,000. Further wall-thickness/insulation verification is unpriced; system-wide modernization is future work. [C]\nOnly the three-assembly immediate recommendation is within the authority reference point. Do not absorb concealed conditions, abatement, controls, downtime, or future modernization.\nRoof: localized seam/flashing deterioration; immediate repair allowance $95,000. Remaining life 3-5 years; future replacement planning range $365,000. [D]\nOnly localized repair is the authority reference point. Do not convert the lifecycle range, possible wet insulation, deck conditions, or weather-dependent observations into a present obligation.\n\nRoles: Eamon may conduct Stages 1-2 and repeat the conditional framework; he may not bind Seller. Arjun coordinates the counterproposal. Reina and Inglewood Board approve economics/annex change. Jelena approves terminology and compliance package. Illinois counsel reviews Illinois property documents, annex and release. Tax adviser/qualified intermediary confirms the federal 1031 identification issue by May 25, 2026; Buyer/lender confirms financing and closing-statement treatment. [F; G]\nTimetable: May 14 call -> obtain evidence and authority path -> circulate only a reviewed written package -> acceptance/reversion at 5:00 p.m. CT on Friday, May 15, 2026 -> preserve scheduled May 29, 2026 closing -> annex use May 30, 2026–July 28, 2026. The May 25 1031 date is a federal timing milestone, not an Illinois or Indiana rule. Illinois matters follow the property situs; Indiana is relevant only to Underhill’s team/financing, not as presumed governing law. Counsel, tax professionals, and lender must confirm their respective consequences. [A; B; F; G]\n7. Operative authorized call position\nExecute this position: no economic concession on the call. First clarify “credit,” obtain item support and lender documentation, and offer source-supported records/access. Only a complete written package, with the executed 60-day annex right, May 29 closing, release, no warranty, no stacking, and required approvals, may reach a final-stage seller contribution shown on the closing statement up to $240,000. Otherwise, stop, preserve the existing agreement, and escalate. [A; B; F]","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX is present at the exact top-level filename and opens as a valid Word document.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Submitted working directory and DOCX package.","grader_hint":"Confirm `coldharbour_counterposition_memo.docx` exists at the top level and can be opened without repair."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered document contains no clipped, missing, corrupted, or unreadable substantive content.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX.","grader_hint":"Render all pages and inspect tables, headers, footers, symbols, and page breaks for loss of content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The complete memorandum, including tables and appendices, is no more than six rendered pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered DOCX page count.","grader_hint":"Count every rendered page; hidden or appendix material counts toward the cap."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document functions as an authorization and call-use memorandum rather than as a generic property summary or inspection recap.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire memorandum.","grader_hint":"A reader should immediately understand the decision being authorized, the negotiation purpose, and how the memo will be used on the call."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material monetary figures, dates, quoted statements, property terms, and report assertions are traceable to identifiable locations in the evidence bundle.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo references compared with the supplied PDF.","grader_hint":"Accept concise page, exhibit, message-date, report-section, or similarly unambiguous references; verify a representative sample across each fact type."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum correctly relates the Thursday call, the closing schedule, and the stated 1031 identification deadline without changing their order or interval.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timeline facts in the memorandum and evidence bundle.","grader_hint":"Compare all stated dates and intervals with the bundle and confirm that the memo preserves the eleven-day urgency."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum advances one coherent counter-position rather than presenting multiple unranked alternatives for the owner to design herself.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation and concession sequence.","grader_hint":"The proposed package may contain stages and conditional branches, but it must represent one integrated negotiating position."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The authorized opening position and principal economic boundary can be found quickly before the supporting analysis.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening portion of the memorandum.","grader_hint":"A call participant should not need to read the entire file to identify the position and the maximum authorized exposure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum expressly defines what it means by “credit” before using that term as part of the counter-position.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Terminology or counter-position language.","grader_hint":"Look for an operative definition tied to the proposed deal mechanics, not merely a statement that the source is ambiguous."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The chosen meaning of “credit” is used consistently in the recommendation, sequence, call language, and authorization limits.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire memorandum.","grader_hint":"Check that purchase-price reduction and closing credit are not silently interchanged after the definition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum distinguishes purchase-price changes, closing credits, seller-paid work, escrows, and non-cash operating concessions where those alternatives have different consequences.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Economic analysis and proposed sequence.","grader_hint":"Credit if the memo recognizes that equal nominal amounts can differ in funding, documentation, lender, tax, or leverage effects without giving unsupported legal conclusions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The buyer’s aggregate re-trade demand is stated as $780,000 with a tolerance of ±$0.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memorandum and buyer demand in the evidence bundle.","grader_hint":"The figure must be exact and clearly attributed to the buyer’s demand rather than to an accepted liability."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any breakdown of the $780,000 demand agrees with the buyer’s own component amounts and sums back to the stated total.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo calculation and buyer correspondence.","grader_hint":"Recalculate any displayed components; do not require a breakdown if the memo does not use one, but award only if the demand is analyzed at component level accurately."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum separates observed defects, recommended future work, budgetary allowances, and buyer-requested amounts rather than treating them as equivalent liabilities.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspection analysis compared with report language.","grader_hint":"Check both the refrigeration and roof discussion for category discipline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Material report qualifications, scope limitations, and timing distinctions that affect negotiation value are preserved.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Inspection report excerpts and memorandum.","grader_hint":"The memo should not convert preliminary, budgetary, lifecycle, or further-investigation language into a present verified cost."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The pattern of the buyer’s requests is analyzed as potentially consistent with lender re-underwriting.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Buyer correspondence, call notes, and memorandum analysis.","grader_hint":"Look for synthesis of timing, wording, documentation requests, and financing references rather than a bare assertion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Lender re-underwriting is labeled as an inference or hypothesis, not represented as a confirmed fact.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Wording throughout the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Fail if the memo states or implies that the lender definitely ordered the re-trade when the bundle does not confirm it."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The proposed call plan tests the lender hypothesis by requesting the relevant confirmation or documentation before changing economics.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call plan and concession sequence.","grader_hint":"The requested proof should be specific enough to distinguish a lender condition from the buyer’s negotiating preference."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum recognizes that the 1031 deadline creates seller timing risk without treating it as a reason to surrender leverage immediately.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation rationale and sequence.","grader_hint":"Credit balanced treatment of deadline exposure and leverage preservation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The call guidance avoids unnecessarily advertising the seller’s 1031 pressure as a negotiating vulnerability.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Proposed external language.","grader_hint":"Internal acknowledgment is appropriate; external scripts should not volunteer desperation or imply that any demand will be accepted to preserve the exchange."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The 60-day loading-annex leaseback or use right is treated as an essential seller objective, consistent with the owner-priority evidence.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner instructions and memorandum.","grader_hint":"It should be a protected term of the package, not a minor item deferred until after price is conceded."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The proposed annex arrangement includes every material term supplied in the evidence bundle that is necessary to make the 60-day use right executable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Proposed leaseback terms and source transaction notes.","grader_hint":"Compare duration, covered area, access, operating responsibility, cost, insurance or risk allocation, and turnover terms to the bundle; do not demand terms absent from the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum explains that an economic concession is the leverage available to secure the annex right and therefore should not be spent first.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation rationale.","grader_hint":"The causal link between sequence and preservation of the seller’s priority must be explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The prior statement that the seller would “make the report items right” is disclosed accurately in the memorandum.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Email or call note and memorandum.","grader_hint":"The exact quotation or a faithful quoted fragment should appear so the compliance reviewer can see the issue being managed."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum does not treat the informal statement as a settled scope, authorized dollar commitment, warranty, or admission of liability.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of the prior communication.","grader_hint":"Look for a professionally defensible distinction between acknowledging the communication and expanding it beyond the evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The call guidance supplies a truthful way to clarify the prior promise without denying that it was made or accusing the buyer of misunderstanding it.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Suggested call language.","grader_hint":"The wording should narrow the commitment to documented, authorized terms while preserving credibility."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The concession sequence begins with clarification and fact testing rather than with a monetary offer.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordered sequence.","grader_hint":"The first stage should resolve the meaning and driver of the demand before value is transferred."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The sequence prevents Eamon from making a binding concession while the meaning of “credit,” the lender role, or the claimed scope remains unresolved.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call authority and stop instructions.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear hold point rather than merely advising caution."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Lower-cost or non-price responses supported by the record are positioned before a broad cash or price concession.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Concession ladder.","grader_hint":"Examples may include access, documentation, assignable rights, targeted cure, escrow structure, or timing terms only where supported by the bundle."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any offered roof or refrigeration response is limited to source-supported scope and does not absorb unrelated, future, optional, or lifecycle work.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Offered scope compared with inspection materials.","grader_hint":"Trace each offered item to the applicable report finding and qualification."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Execution of the 60-day annex arrangement is required before or simultaneously with any material economic concession.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Sequence and conditions.","grader_hint":"A promise to negotiate the annex later is not sufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Concessions are presented as a conditional package rather than as independent gifts that the buyer may retain while rejecting the seller’s reciprocal terms.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Counter-position language.","grader_hint":"Look for explicit if/then, package, simultaneous-document, or contingent-acceptance mechanics."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The sequence releases value incrementally, with later stages unavailable unless the conditions for earlier stages are satisfied.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Concession ladder and branch logic.","grader_hint":"Stages should operate as real gates, not merely as a numbered list of offers all available at once."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Each material seller concession identifies a corresponding buyer commitment or risk reduction.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Concession matrix or narrative.","grader_hint":"Reciprocity may include leaseback execution, scope release, closing certainty, lender confirmation, schedule protection, or another source-supported return."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Any monetary concession is reserved for the final authorized stage rather than anchoring the opening response.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordered counter-position.","grader_hint":"The sequence may discuss a ceiling internally, but the initial external move should not simply concede price or cash."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The maximum proposed seller exposure does not exceed the lowest applicable source-supported limit among authority, verified scope, and the buyer’s demand.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authorization evidence, inspection support, buyer demand, and memo calculations.","grader_hint":"Recalculate the cap using the controlling limits in the bundle and confirm consistent treatment of cash, escrow, and seller-paid work."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package prevents stacking or double recovery across a credit, repair payment, escrow, warranty assignment, or other remedy for the same condition.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Package terms and exclusions.","grader_hint":"Look for offset, election, exclusive-remedy, or equivalent anti-duplication language suitable for broker-level recommendation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The offer has a source-consistent acceptance deadline or reversion mechanism that protects the existing deal if the package is not accepted.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Proposed timing and existing agreement terms.","grader_hint":"The memo should not leave an enhanced concession open indefinitely or imply that the original contract is waived without acceptance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The “never give” guidance prohibits an unconditional purchase-price reduction or closing credit before the annex right and package conditions are secured.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation guardrails.","grader_hint":"The prohibition must be explicit enough for the covering broker to apply during the call."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The “never give” guidance prohibits an uncapped or open-ended obligation to repair report items.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation guardrails.","grader_hint":"Accept wording that requires defined scope and a stated cap or otherwise bars unlimited exposure."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The “never give” guidance prohibits new broad assurances about the roof, refrigeration system, or future performance beyond the supplied evidence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation guardrails.","grader_hint":"Look for protection against creating a new condition warranty or guaranteeing useful life."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The “never give” guidance protects contract, closing, release, and documentation safeguards that the evidence shows remain material to the seller.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Existing transaction terms and memo guardrails.","grader_hint":"Credit only for safeguards grounded in the bundle; the memo need not reproduce the agreement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The “never give” guidance expressly bars sacrificing or deferring the 60-day annex right in exchange for keeping the sale alive.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Owner priorities and memo guardrails.","grader_hint":"The instruction must resolve this tradeoff rather than merely call the annex important."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum gives Eamon usable opening language that acknowledges the demand without accepting its premise or amount.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call script or talk track.","grader_hint":"The language should be close enough to spoken wording that a covering broker can use it directly."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The call plan contains a compact set of purposeful questions that can determine scope, decision-maker, financing driver, and required timing.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call questions.","grader_hint":"Questions should obtain information that changes the authorized branch; generic rapport questions do not count."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"At least one proposed question directly identifies whether a lender, lender consultant, or underwriting condition is driving the request and what evidence supports it.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call questions.","grader_hint":"The question should seek verifiable detail rather than accuse the buyer of using the lender as a pretext."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"At least one proposed question requires the buyer to state whether “credit” means a price reduction, a closing credit, seller-paid work, or another mechanism.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call questions.","grader_hint":"The question must pin down mechanics before negotiation proceeds."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum supplies an executable response if the buyer substantiates a lender-driven requirement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conditional call branches.","grader_hint":"The branch should identify the next permitted offer, required reciprocity, and stopping point."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum supplies a different executable response if the buyer cannot substantiate a lender-driven requirement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conditional call branches.","grader_hint":"The weaker-evidence branch should preserve more seller value and not default to the same concession."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum tells Eamon how to respond if Underhill insists on the full $780,000 immediately.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call branches and authority limits.","grader_hint":"The response should state what he may say, what he may not agree to, and whether he pauses or escalates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R51","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum tells Eamon how to respond if Underhill uses the closing schedule or the seller’s timing pressure to demand an immediate answer.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Call branches.","grader_hint":"The branch should preserve the deadline without authorizing an improvised concession."},{"rubric_item_id":"R52","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Negotiation, approval, compliance review, drafting, and specialist-advice responsibilities are assigned consistently with the roles and authority shown in the evidence bundle.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Responsibility assignments and source authority records.","grader_hint":"Confirm that no participant is given authority the bundle withholds and that essential actions have a named owner."},{"rubric_item_id":"R53","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The operational timetable works backward from the Thursday call and relevant transaction deadlines, with all proposed milestones occurring in a feasible order.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Memo timeline and evidence-bundle dates.","grader_hint":"Check sequencing of approval, call, documentation, any acceptance period, closing, annex use, and 1031 milestones."},{"rubric_item_id":"R54","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum states which matters Eamon may resolve on the call and which require owner, compliance, counsel, tax, lender, or other specialist confirmation.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authority and escalation instructions.","grader_hint":"Instructions should be concrete enough to prevent unauthorized agreement while avoiding blanket referral of the whole negotiation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R55","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The jurisdiction discussion distinguishes federal 1031 timing from state-specific brokerage, property, documentation, or closing considerations.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction discussion and source compliance material.","grader_hint":"The memo should not describe the federal identification deadline as an Illinois or Indiana rule."},{"rubric_item_id":"R56","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Illinois discussion correctly connects the property’s location and the Illinois-specific source material to the proposed transaction handling.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction section and evidence bundle.","grader_hint":"Check that the memo identifies the practical Illinois implication supported by the bundle rather than merely naming the state."},{"rubric_item_id":"R57","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Indiana discussion correctly limits the relevance of the buyer’s headquarters, financing activity, or Indiana-based participants to the implications supported by the evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction section and evidence bundle.","grader_hint":"The memo should explain the relevant Indiana connection without assuming Indiana law governs the Illinois real estate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R58","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum does not state definitive legal or tax conclusions and identifies the specific points that need confirmation by qualified counsel or tax advisers.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction, 1031, and documentation language.","grader_hint":"A generic disclaimer alone is insufficient if substantive text elsewhere gives categorical legal or tax advice."},{"rubric_item_id":"R59","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum prioritizes the transaction’s material risks and links each priority risk to a mitigation embedded in the recommended sequence.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Risk analysis and counter-position.","grader_hint":"Expected risks include leverage loss, annex access, unsupported scope, authority, schedule, and documentation; credit synthesis rather than a disconnected risk list."},{"rubric_item_id":"R60","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum records the authorized negotiating position as a controlled change from the earlier informal communication and identifies what prior understanding is being clarified or superseded.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Authorization language and treatment of the prior promise.","grader_hint":"The artifact should create a reviewable decision record, not merely offer private advice."},{"rubric_item_id":"R61","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A broker unfamiliar with the transaction can use the memorandum during the call without asking the author to supply missing order, wording, authority, branches, or stop conditions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire rendered memorandum.","grader_hint":"Judge practical usability under call pressure; concise tables, scripts, and visual hierarchy may help, but no specific layout is required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R62","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is professionally concise, visually navigable, and internally consistent in terminology, figures, dates, recommendation, and authority limits.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire rendered memorandum.","grader_hint":"Check for contradictions between summary, analysis, sequence, scripts, and guardrails, as well as whether the six-page product remains usable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R63","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum ends with the operative authorized call position or decision boundary rather than an unresolved list of alternatives or a generic next-steps conclusion.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final substantive portion of the memorandum.","grader_hint":"The final takeaway should reinforce the one position Eamon is to execute."},{"rubric_item_id":"R64","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The memorandum invents any unsupported dollar amount, valuation, repair estimate, deadline, property fact, legal requirement, tax result, or deal term.","weight":-8.0,"polarity":"penalty","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Entire memorandum compared with the complete evidence bundle.","grader_hint":"Apply once if any material factual or numerical term is created rather than traced to the source. Do not apply merely because the memo makes a clearly labeled negotiation inference or professional recommendation."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"A commercial real estate broker must convert a complete but mixed transaction record into an executable negotiating position under deadline pressure. The memorandum will be used by a covering broker on the buyer call and reviewed by the seller’s compliance function.","difficulty_sources":["Sequencing individually defensible concessions so the seller does not surrender the only leverage available for the essential post-closing annex right.","Converting mixed reports, correspondence, authority records, and deadlines into one internally consistent and executable call position.","Handling an ambiguous deal term and a prior informal promise without making unsupported legal, technical, lender, or tax assertions.","Separating report-supported facts from a defensible but unconfirmed inference of lender re-underwriting.","Applying Illinois, Indiana, and federal considerations only to the parts of the transaction they actually govern."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_artifact":{"format":"A single searchable PDF evidence bundle assembled from mixed workplace records.","content_requirements":["Include an executed agreement abstract or transaction summary showing price, closing schedule, current amendment status, inspection-related rights, amendment mechanics, and any relevant survival or release provisions.","Include an owner-priority record establishing that uninterrupted use of a specified loading annex for 60 days after closing is operationally essential and more important than preserving every dollar of headline price.","Include roof and refrigeration report excerpts that distinguish observed conditions, immediate recommended work, future or lifecycle recommendations, budgetary estimates, exclusions, and requests for further investigation.","Include the buyer’s $780,000 re-trade and enough component detail for the components to reconcile exactly to the aggregate request.","Include correspondence that uses “credit” in at least two materially different senses: purchase-price reduction and a seller credit shown at closing.","Include the broker’s informal statement that the seller will make the report items right, together with surrounding context showing that no scope, amount, remedy, or authority was fixed.","Include buyer communications and call notes whose timing and wording support, but do not prove, an inference of lender re-underwriting.","Include a current authority record identifying the seller’s maximum authorized economic exposure, matters the covering broker may discuss, and matters requiring owner, compliance, counsel, tax, or other specialist approval.","Include source-supported non-price or lower-cost responses, such as targeted cure choices, access, documentation, assignable warranties, escrow mechanics, or timing accommodations, without labeling a preferred sequence.","Include all material terms needed to make the 60-day annex arrangement executable, including the applicable space, dates, access, operating responsibilities, cost treatment, insurance or risk allocation, and turnover requirements.","Include the seller’s 1031 identification date, closing date, Thursday call date, and other operative milestones in a mutually consistent timeline.","Include concise compliance material addressing the federal character of the 1031 deadline, the Illinois situs of the real estate and relevant transaction handling, and the limited Indiana relevance created by the buyer’s location or financing activity.","Include page labels, exhibit labels, message dates, or comparable anchors that permit precise citation."]},"evidence_relationships":["The buyer-demand components must sum exactly to $780,000.","The supported negotiation ceiling is the lowest applicable limit among the buyer’s demand, source-supported current scope, and the seller’s authorized maximum exposure; remedies addressing the same condition cannot be stacked when calculating exposure.","Observed conditions, immediate work, future work, budget allowances, and buyer demands must remain separate categories; a report estimate is not automatically a seller liability.","The 60-day annex right is the seller’s priority term, so the viable sequence preserves monetary or price movement as leverage until that right is executed or simultaneously documented.","The lender-driver conclusion must remain an inference because the bundle contains suggestive communications but no definitive lender directive.","Any enhanced seller remedy must be conditional on reciprocal buyer commitments, must prevent double recovery, and must expire or revert if not accepted under source-consistent timing.","The prior informal promise must be acknowledged and narrowed through accurate clarification; the gold must neither deny the statement nor transform it into an uncapped warranty.","Illinois relevance follows the property situs and supplied transaction-compliance record. Indiana relevance is limited to the buyer or financing connection shown in the source and must not be used to claim that Indiana law governs the Illinois property.","Federal 1031 timing must be distinguished from state-specific transaction considerations, with legal and tax conclusions reserved for qualified specialists."],"intended_solution_behavior":{"position":"Produce one integrated, call-ready counter-position that begins by clarifying the requested remedy and testing the financing driver, moves through source-supported lower-cost responses, conditions any meaningful concession on execution of the 60-day annex arrangement and other reciprocal protections, and reserves a capped monetary response for the final authorized stage.","instructional_quality":"A covering broker unfamiliar with the file must be able to identify the opening language, questions, permitted branches, escalation points, authority ceiling, reciprocal terms, and non-negotiable prohibitions without contacting the author.","must_not_claim":["That lender re-underwriting is confirmed.","That the informal promise established a binding scope, amount, warranty, or admission.","That every report recommendation is an immediate defect or seller obligation.","That Indiana law governs the Illinois real estate merely because the buyer or financing team is based there.","That the memorandum supplies definitive legal, engineering, lender, or tax advice."],"intended_verdict":"A strong submission authorizes a single bounded position, preserves the annex leverage through the ordering of concessions, handles the ambiguous term and prior promise professionally, and can be executed by the covering broker under the stated deadline."},"gold_construction_checks":["Trace every figure, date, quoted statement, and transaction term to the PDF.","Recalculate the buyer-demand total and the maximum aggregate seller exposure.","Confirm that no remedy is counted twice.","Walk every branch to ensure the broker always has a permitted response or a clear stop-and-escalate instruction.","Render the final DOCX and confirm it remains within six pages without clipped or unreadable content.","Review the final paragraph to ensure it ends on the operative authorized position."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_transaction_evidence","filename":"coldharbour_transaction_evidence.pdf","purpose":"Complete mixed-format evidence bundle containing the transaction terms, inspection materials, correspondence, call notes, authority limits, deadline information, leaseback requirements, and jurisdiction-related compliance material needed to prepare the counter-position.","required":true,"discovery":"Read the full bundle, including embedded report excerpts, email chains, notes, and transaction summaries."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"counterposition_memo","filename":"coldharbour_counterposition_memo.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A call-ready counter-position and concession-sequence memorandum for owner authorization and compliance review.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be written to the top level of the working directory under the exact filename; must not exceed six pages including tables and appendices; must present one coherent counter-position; all figures, dates, property terms, and report assertions must be traceable to the supplied evidence bundle."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"professional_judgment"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"real_estate_brokers","sector":"real_estate_rental_leasing","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":5.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"The reference memorandum must be drafted by a commercial real estate transaction specialist and independently reviewed by a second broker or transaction attorney for source fidelity, negotiation sequencing, authority discipline, jurisdictional framing, and call usability. Reviewers must render the DOCX, verify its page count, trace all material facts to the supplied PDF, and walk every conditional call branch.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The work product is a broker-level negotiation memorandum, not a legal opinion, tax opinion, engineering assessment, or lender commitment. More than one stylistic presentation can satisfy the rubric, but the economic sequence and authorization boundaries must remain source-supported."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:40+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:40+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:40+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:40+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:21:40+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/510b5c3c8b722b3e","declared_deliverables":["coldharbour_counterposition_memo.docx"]};
